---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ObfuscatedEmail from '../../components/ObfuscatedEmail.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="Transportation Committee" description="BWNA's Transportation Committee identifies and advocates for Beaumont-Wilshire's transportation concerns, with pedestrian, cyclist, and driver safety as its priority.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Transportation Committee</h1>
      <p>Safer streets for walking, biking, and driving in Beaumont-Wilshire</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container content-width">
      <p>
        This committee works to identify and advocate for the transportation-related concerns of
        our neighborhood. Pedestrian, cyclist, and driver safety are their priority. The
        committee brings its concerns to the attention of the Portland Bureau of Transportation
        to seek solutions.
      </p>

      <div class="map-callout">
        <h2>Neighborhood Transportation Map</h2>
        <p>
          Explore greenways, Safe Routes to School, High Crash Network streets, and crash records
          across Beaumont-Wilshire on the committee's interactive map.
        </p>
        <a href={`${base}transportation-map`} class="btn btn-secondary">View the map</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container content-width">
      <h2>Getting to Know Your BWNA Transportation Volunteer</h2>
      <p class="byline">By Graeme Rudd, BWNA Transportation Committee Chair</p>
      <p>
        Hi neighbors, I'm Graeme Rudd. I recently volunteered to support BWNA as its
        Transportation Committee chair, and I'd like to introduce myself and share what I've been
        working on.
      </p>

      <h3>A Little About Me</h3>
      <p>
        I spent about 14 years in federal service, mostly in the military. I served as a Green
        Beret, including time with a technology lab and as an intelligence analyst working with
        geographic information systems (GIS). That background shapes my approach: I like to
        start with a clear picture of what's happening on the ground.
      </p>

      <h3>Why I'm Doing This</h3>
      <p>
        We often hear there's no money for the transportation improvements our neighborhood
        needs. But there may be funding allocations or programs out there to help meet those
        needs. So, my first goal is simple: to understand our neighborhood's transportation
        picture and find out what resources might be available.
      </p>

      <h3>What I've Been Working On</h3>
      <p>
        I've had two helpful conversations with representatives from the Portland Bureau of
        Transportation (PBOT), who pointed me to data that clarified our neighborhood's
        transportation realities and where to dig deeper. I've started putting that data onto an
        <a href={`${base}transportation-map`}>interactive map</a> showing:
      </p>
      <ul class="spaced-list">
        <li>
          B-W neighborhood greenways (streets that prioritize people walking, bicycling, and
          rolling).
        </li>
        <li>
          Roads on the city's High Crash Network (HCN), which includes NE Fremont Street. Visit
          <a href="https://www.portland.gov/transportation/vision-zero/high-crash-network-streets-and-intersections">this PBOT page</a>
          for more info about Portland's HCN.
        </li>
        <li>Safe Routes to School (safe, accessible routes for students).</li>
        <li>Intersections that crash data shows are most dangerous.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        My hope is to build this into something neighbors can explore so we share an
        understanding of our current baseline and where improvements are needed.
      </p>

      <h3>Where This Could Lead</h3>
      <p>
        With a clearer picture, I'd like to see whether our needs line up with existing
        programs, such as Safe Routes to School, that could help fund improvements. At a minimum,
        this work should help us show PBOT and our elected representatives where our
        neighborhood needs the most help.
      </p>

      <h3>How You Can Be Part of It</h3>
      <p>
        Data only tells part of the story. I'm working with other committee members on ways to
        gather community input so we can advocate for what the neighborhood needs most, backed by
        data and your insights.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'll share more as the map comes together. Meanwhile, if you have thoughts about
        transportation in the neighborhood, I'd love to hear them. Email me at
        <ObfuscatedEmail email="pdx.stmptwn@gmail.com" />.
      </p>

      <p class="bio">
        Graeme Rudd spent about 14 years in the military with multiple deployments overseas.
        During his service he was assigned to a military lab that assessed new and emerging
        technology, which is how he entered the Cybersecurity and Deep Tech space. He later
        attended Lewis &amp; Clark Law School and earned his JD (Juris Doctor) degree, then
        co-founded two businesses focused on new and emerging technologies. After over a decade
        as a geographic nomad, he looks forward to raising his family in the Beaumont-Wilshire
        neighborhood.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container content-width">
      <h2>Get involved</h2>
      <p>
        If you're interested in assisting with the important work of this committee,
        <ObfuscatedEmail email="pdx.stmptwn@gmail.com" label="contact the Transportation Committee Chair" />.
      </p>
      <p><a href={`${base}committees`}>&larr; All committees</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .content-width > h2:not(:first-child) {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }

  .content-width > h3:not(:first-child) {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .map-callout {
    background: var(--color-primary-light);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin: var(--spacing-xl) 0;
  }

  .map-callout h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .byline {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-text-light);
  }

  .bio {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding-top: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
